Brydge was a B2B platform for trade across Africa. Merchants, importers, exporters and suppliers used it to invoice, pay and get paid across borders. It already had active users, and it was preparing to raise money and relaunch.

The product had grown without a clear structure. Users struggled to find their way around and sometimes needed help with basic tasks. It didn’t work well on mobile, and every new feature risked breaking an existing one.

## What I did

With a little over two months to design and build, I started with the flows money moves through. I reorganised navigation into clear sections (payments, accounts, customers, bills) so new features had somewhere to go. I redesigned the multi-currency payment flow as a short sequence of steps that works on a phone as well as on desktop, and designed invoicing and a customer directory around it.

To move fast, we skipped most low-fidelity work and went straight to Figma prototypes, refining the payment flow first before carrying the changes across the platform.

